+### Independent work performed (no reporter code/artifacts reused)
+
+- **Theorem A — hard-child one-ply drop ≤ 1, CONFIRMED and STRENGTHENED.** The report proves it on a principal-variation transition under F(H)=F(P)−1. I drop that assumption: for ANY incomparable pair at P with harder outcome H (F(H)=max child F), minimax gives F(P)=1+min_pairs max(child F) ≤ 1+F(H), so F(P)−F(H) ≤ 1; and H is a transitively-closed child, so e(H)≤e(P) ⇒ L(H)≤L(P). Hence δ(P)−δ(H)=(F(P)−F(H))−(L(P)−L(H)) ≤ 1 for all n and all finite posets. Fresh from-scratch solver `/tmp/opencode/exec_verify_defect_20261123.py`: exhaustive over all posets on n≤6 (4,231 at n=5; 130,023 at n=6), hard-child drop distribution {−1,0,1}, zero drops >1.
+- **REFINEMENT — a genuine correction.** The same distribution shows δ can RISE by 1 on a hard child at slack (non-F-optimal) nodes where F(H)=F(P): 720 events at n=5, 81,960 at n=6; witness n=5 succ=(22,0,0,2,2), F=4, δ=0, compare (2,3) with child F=(2,4), hard child F=4=F(P) and δ=1. So "δ is nonincreasing / defect heals monotonically" requires the F-optimality hypothesis F(H)=F(P)−1; it is FALSE at slack nodes. Does not refute the report (which restricts Theorem A to principal variation) but matters for any layer-indexed defect-certificate argument. **Theorem B** (drop ≥2 needs a reachable δ≥2 parent) confirmed as immediate from δ(C)≥0.
+- **Exhaustive census — CONFIRMED and STRENGTHENED.** Independently written Go solver `/tmp/opencode/exec_n7_delta_census.go` (own transitive closure, own 2⁷ subset-DP extension count, own memoised minimax): F(A₇)=13, all 6,129,859 posets on 7 elements enumerated, δ histogram {0: 4,847,459; 1: 1,282,400}, max δ=1, ZERO with δ≥2 (witness succ=(0,0,3,1,9,0,3), e=224, F=9). This covers ALL n=7 posets, a strict superset of height-S(7) optimal-tree states, so the report's n≤7 claim follows. Also independently confirmed curator witness K=(30,16,8,0,0,18) has e=16, F=5, δ=1, and g(A_n)=true for n≤6.
+- **Preserved as unverified, not asserted false:** the report's 3,044,007-state / 38.3M-transition budgeted n=7 optimal-tree scan (my all-posets census is a different, stronger check, not a replay). n=8 exact scan infeasible here by my own resource check (F(A₈) visits all 431,723,379 posets ≈20 GB vs 12 GB available). General-poset δ=2 (W⊕W e=64,F=8; n=17 prime family) is off the optimal tree; reachability/selection is the open gap. No transfer to an S(n) upper bound without a reduction; sparsity/Mahaney and PSPACE barriers remain.
